---
// Privacy policy, from ../content/privacy-policy.md (draft 1, written from the code). The deck's
// [IF ENABLED: GA4] and [IF ENABLED: META] blocks follow src/data/site.ts: they show only once that platform's ID
// is set, so the page always describes what the site really loads. The gaps were filled 2026-11-09 from the
// owner's facts (the operating company, Wyoming) and Ergonomc LLC's own policy, checked against the code here:
// retention from worker/addons/events.ts and worker/ga4.ts, and no Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track
// handling anywhere in src/features/tracking/ or worker/. Ergonomc LLC is named on the legal pages only.
import LegalLayout from '../../components/blog/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const ga4 = site.tracking.ga4MeasurementId !== '';
const meta = site.tracking.metaPixelId !== '';
const email = site.contact.email;
const others = [ga4 && 'Google', meta && 'Meta'].filter(Boolean) as string[];
const othersOr = others.join(' or ');

const sections = [
  { id: 'in-brief', label: 'In brief' },
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-you-send', label: 'What you send us' },
  { id: 'browsing', label: 'What the site records' },
  { id: 'why', label: 'Why we use it' },
  { id: 'processors', label: 'Who processes your data' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies and what we store' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'How long we hold data' },
  { id: 'switch-off', label: 'How to switch tracking off' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Security' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'links', label: 'Sites we link to' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'When this policy changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Lawyer SEO Expert"
  description="What lawyerseoexpert.com collects, why, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to switch tracking off."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  h1="Privacy policy"
  updated="2026-11-09"
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="in-brief">In brief</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>When you send us a form, we keep what you typed so we can reply. It is emailed to our own inboxes and stored in a database run on Cloudflare.</li>
    <li>When you browse, the site measures visits and leads so we know which pages and ads work. Today that measurement goes to Reddit{others.length > 0 && <>, and to {others.join(' and ')} as well</>}.</li>
    <li>We do not sell your details for money. We do send limited data to advertising platforms, as set out below.</li>
    <li>You can switch the site's tracking off in your browser (see <a href="#switch-off">how to switch tracking off</a>).</li>
    <li>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
  <p>Lawyer SEO Expert is a brand of Ergonomc LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company, and this is its site. In this policy "we" means that business. Our postal address is under <a href="#contact">Contact</a>. Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="what-you-send">What you send us</h2>
  <p><strong>Through the contact form.</strong> Your name and email (required), your firm's website, and optionally your phone number and a message. Some pages also send which page or practice area the form was on.</p>
  <p><strong>Alongside the form, automatically.</strong> The page you sent it from, any campaign tags in the link you arrived by (such as utm_source), a Reddit click ID when a Reddit ad brought you here, your screen size, your country (as Cloudflare reports it) and a one-way scrambled version of your IP address. The scrambled IP is made with a secret key and is used only to stop the same sender flooding the form.</p>
  <p><strong>Spam checks.</strong> The form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, a check that tells people from bots without a puzzle in most cases. Turnstile is run by Cloudflare and processes technical details of your browser to do this. A hidden empty field and a minimum time on the page are also checked.</p>
  <p><strong>When you book a call.</strong> Booking happens in a Calendly window. Your name, email and any answers you give are collected by Calendly and stay in Calendly, under <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Calendly's privacy policy</a>. Our database records only that a booking happened, which page it came from and how you reached the site (campaign tags, the referring site, the first page you landed on). No name, email or IP address is stored with that record.</p>
  <p><strong>When you email us.</strong> Your message reaches our mailbox at {email} and is kept there like any business email.</p>

  <h2 id="browsing">What the site records when you browse</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Visit counts.</strong> Page views, form sends and booking-dialog opens are recorded as events with the page, the time and any campaign tags. These records hold no IP address and no contact details.</li>
    <li><strong>Broken pages.</strong> When a page is missing or fails, we record the address requested, the error and the referring page, so we can fix the link.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs.</strong> Cloudflare keeps short-lived server logs for the site. Our code is built and tested not to write contact details into them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="why">Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer your enquiry and discuss working together.</li>
    <li>To measure which pages, searches and ads bring enquiries, and to report conversions to the ad platforms below.</li>
    <li>To keep the site and the form safe from spam and abuse.</li>
    <li>To find and fix broken pages.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Our services are for law firms in the United States. If you visit from the EU or the UK, data protection law asks us to name the legal basis for each use:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Answering your enquiry:</strong> steps you asked us to take before we might work together.</li>
    <li><strong>Measuring pages and ads, reporting conversions, stopping spam and fixing broken pages:</strong> our legitimate interest in running and growing the business. You can object at any time, and you can switch the site's tracking off yourself (see <a href="#switch-off">how to switch tracking off</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Keeping or handing over data when the law says we must:</strong> a legal duty.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="processors">Who processes your data for us</h2>
  <p><strong>Cloudflare.</strong> Hosts the site, runs the form and database, sends lead emails, and runs Turnstile. Leads and events are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database located in eastern North America. <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">How Cloudflare handles data</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Lead emails.</strong> Each form sent is emailed to the business's own inboxes through Cloudflare's email service, with your address set as the reply address. If sending fails, the site retries for about three days.</p>
  <p><strong>Reddit.</strong> We use the Reddit Pixel (ID {site.tracking.redditPixelId}) in your browser and Reddit's Conversions API from our server. Reddit receives page visits, content views and form sends, with a conversion ID, the page address, your IP address and browser details, Reddit's click ID if you came from a Reddit ad, and Reddit's own browser identifier. When you send the form, Reddit also receives your email and phone number in scrambled form (a SHA-256 hash, not the plain text), so it can match the lead to an ad click. <a href="https://www.reddit.com/policies/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Reddit's privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Calendly.</strong> Runs the booking window (see what you send us, "When you book a call").</p>
  {ga4 && (
    <p><strong>Google Analytics.</strong> Google Analytics 4 measures visits through a Google tag served via Cloudflare, which sets Google's <code>_ga</code> cookies. When you send a form or book a call, our server reports that event to Google with the Analytics visitor ID from those cookies, your IP address (which Google uses to estimate location), your device type and the campaign tags. No name, email or phone number is sent to Google. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p>
  )}
  {meta && (
    <p><strong>Meta (Facebook and Instagram).</strong> The Meta Pixel in your browser and Meta's Conversions API from our server receive page visits and form sends, with your IP address and browser details, Meta's browser cookies (<code>_fbp</code>, <code>_fbc</code>), a random visitor ID we create, and, for a form sent, your email and phone number in scrambled (hashed) form. <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" rel="noopener">Meta's privacy policy</a>.</p>
  )}
  <p>We share data beyond these services only if the law requires it, to protect our rights or safety, or as part of a sale or transfer of the business.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and what the site stores in your browser</h2>
  <table class="lse-stack" role="table">
    <thead role="rowgroup"><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Name</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Where</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Set by</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">What it is for</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">How long</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody role="rowgroup">
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>lse_notrack</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Cookie</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">This site</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Switches tracking off on this browser</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">1 year</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>rct_cid</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Local storage</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">This site</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Reddit ad click ID, so a later form can be matched to the click</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">90 days</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>rct_mk</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Local storage</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">This site</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Scrambled email and phone after a form, for Reddit matching</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">90 days</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>lse_utm</code>, <code>lse_touch</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Local storage</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">This site</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Campaign tags, referring site and first landing page</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">90 days</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>_rdt_uuid</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Cookie</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">Reddit</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Reddit's browser identifier</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">Set by Reddit</td></tr>
      {ga4 && <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Cookie</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">Google</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Analytics visitor and session</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">Set by Google</td></tr>}
      {meta && <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>_fbp</code>, <code>_fbc</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Cookie</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">Meta</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Meta's browser and click identifiers</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">Set by Meta</td></tr>}
      {meta && <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>lse_vid</code>, <code>lse_fbc</code>, <code>lse_fbmk</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Local storage</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">This site</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Random visitor ID, Meta click ID and scrambled contact details for Meta matching</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">90 days</td></tr>}
      {meta && <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name"><code>lse_meta_test</code></td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Session storage</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">This site</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">A test code used only by us when testing</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">Until the tab closes</td></tr>}
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name">Cloudflare and Turnstile</td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Cookie or storage</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">Cloudflare</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Security and bot checks</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">Set by Cloudflare</td></tr>
      <tr role="row"><td role="cell" data-label="Name">Calendly</td><td role="cell" data-label="Where">Cookie</td><td role="cell" data-label="Set by">Calendly</td><td role="cell" data-label="What it is for">Running the booking window</td><td role="cell" data-label="How long">Set by Calendly</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we hold your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Form enquiries that don't lead to work:</strong> kept for 24 months after our last contact with you, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>If you become a client:</strong> your enquiry is kept while we work together, then for as long as our agreement or tax and accounting law requires.</li>
    <li><strong>Visit events and booking records:</strong> deleted automatically after 180 days.</li>
    {ga4 && <li><strong>Google Analytics send records:</strong> a short record that stops the same event being counted twice, deleted after 30 days.</li>}
    <li><strong>Broken-page records:</strong> these hold no contact details and no IP address, only the address asked for, the error, the referring page and a count. Nothing deletes them on a timer. We keep them while they help us fix links.</li>
    <li><strong>Browser storage set by this site:</strong> expires after 90 days, or when you clear it.</li>
    <li><strong>Data held by Reddit, Calendly{others.length > 0 ? `, ${others.join(', ')}` : ''} and Cloudflare:</strong> kept under each company's own policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you ask us to delete your data sooner, we will, unless the law says we must keep it.</p>

  <h2 id="switch-off">How to switch tracking off</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>On this site:</strong> visit <a href="/?notrack=1">lawyerseoexpert.com/?notrack=1</a>. That sets the <code>lse_notrack</code> cookie for a year, and the site then loads no ad pixels, records no visit events and sends nothing to Reddit{others.length > 0 && <> or {othersOr}</>} from our server.{ga4 && <> Google's own page tag, which Cloudflare adds to each page, still counts the visit. <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a> stops it.</>} Forms still work and still reach us, marked as not to be counted. To switch tracking back on, visit <a href="/?notrack=0">lawyerseoexpert.com/?notrack=0</a>. Clearing your cookies removes the setting.</li>
    <li><strong>In your browser:</strong> block third-party cookies, clear site data or use a content blocker.</li>
    <li><strong>With the platforms:</strong> Reddit{others.length > 0 && <>, {others.join(' and ')}</>} each offer ad settings in your account.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track.</strong> The site does not read either signal. Pages and the tracking described above run the same whether or not your browser sends one. To switch the site's tracking off, use the link above.</p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it or delete it, or object to how we use it. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We may need to confirm it is you before acting. Depending on where you live, you may have further rights, including to opt out of the sharing of personal information for targeted advertising.</p>
  <p><strong>US state privacy laws.</strong> California and several other states give their residents set rights: to know what we collect and why, to get a copy, to correct it, to delete it, and to opt out of its sale or of its sharing for targeted advertising. These laws may treat what the site sends to Reddit{others.length > 0 && <> and {others.join(' and ')}</>} for advertising as a sale or as sharing, even though nobody pays us for it. To opt out of that, switch the site's tracking off with the link above, on each browser you use. We answer these requests from anyone, wherever you live.</p>
  <p><strong>How to ask.</strong> Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and say what you'd like us to do. We reply within 45 days. If we need longer, we'll tell you why and how much longer, within the time the law allows. We usually confirm it is you by writing back to the email address we already hold. An agent you appoint can ask for you, and we'll ask them for proof that you appointed them.</p>
  <p><strong>No penalty, and a right to appeal.</strong> Using these rights doesn't change how we treat you. If we turn a request down, we'll say why. You can appeal by replying to that answer, and we'll respond within 45 days. If we turn the appeal down too, you can contact your state attorney general.</p>
  <p><strong>If you are in the EU or the UK.</strong> You also have the right to limit how we use your data and to get it in a format you can take elsewhere. You can complain to your local data protection authority, though we'd like the chance to put things right first. Our providers handle your data in the United States and other countries.</p>
  <h3 id="california">If you live in California</h3>
  <p>The site collects these kinds of personal information, from you and from your browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> your name, email, phone number and IP address, ad click IDs, and the browser IDs in the cookies and storage listed above.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional details:</strong> your firm's website, and the practice area when a page sends it.</li>
    <li><strong>Internet activity:</strong> pages viewed, forms sent, booking-window opens, campaign tags, the referring site and your screen size.</li>
    <li><strong>Rough location:</strong> your country, as Cloudflare reports it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use them for the reasons under <a href="#why">why we use it</a> and keep them as <a href="#retention">how long we hold your data</a> sets out. They go to the services under <a href="#processors">who processes your data</a>. Identifiers and internet activity go to Reddit{others.length > 0 && <> and {others.join(' and ')}</>} for advertising, which California law may call sharing. We don't sell personal information for money, and we don't collect sensitive personal information to infer things about you.</p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>Data travels over encrypted connections. The database and email run on Cloudflare's infrastructure. IP addresses are stored only in scrambled form. No system is perfectly secure, and we will tell you if the law requires it after a breach.</p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>This site is for businesses. It is not meant for anyone under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their data. If you think a child has sent us their details, email us and we will delete them.</p>

  <h2 id="links">Sites we link to</h2>
  <p>Pages link to other sites, such as Google results or our booking page. Their own privacy policies apply there.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">When this policy changes</h2>
  <p>When the site changes how it handles data, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Email us about your data: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>
  <p>Lawyer SEO Expert, a brand of Ergonomc LLC<br>30 N Gould St Ste R, Sheridan, WY 82801</p>
</LegalLayout>
